**Problem.** Check on an essence pouch says "There are 3 pure essence in this pouch." and, when empty, "There are no essences in this pouch.". The OSRS lines spell the number out and name the essence kind, and RuneLite's Ess Pouch plugin (Plugin Hub, by Adam-) tracks the pouches from exactly that form:

```java
Pattern.compile("^There (?:is|are) ([a-z-]+)(?: pure| daeyalt| guardian)? essences? in this pouch\\.$");
```

with "no", "one" ... "forty" mapped to numbers ([Adam-/runelite-plugins](https://github.com/Adam-/runelite-plugins), `EssPouchPlugin.java`). With the current wording the plugin never learns what a pouch holds.

**Change.** Check sends "There are three pure essences in this pouch.", "There is one essence in this pouch." (rune essence has no qualifier), "There are twenty-seven guardian essences in this pouch." (number words, hyphenated above twenty), and "There is no essence in this pouch." for an empty pouch (Check and Empty). The kind comes from the stored essence's cache name, as before.

**Tests.** None added (message text only). Compared with the plugin's pattern and number map. Not re-checked in game on this branch.

**Caveats.** Numbers of 100 or more fall back to digits; no pouch holds that many.

**Release note.** Checking an essence pouch uses the OSRS wording, so RuneLite's Ess Pouch plugin can track pouch contents.

